---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import results from '../../../../../research/market-lens/results.json';
import prospective from '../../../../../research/market-lens/prospective-manifest.json';
const number = (value: number) => value.toFixed(5);
const percent = (value: number) => `${(value * 100).toFixed(2)}%`;
const names = { unconditional: 'Unconditional baseline', persistence: 'Persistence baseline', taOnly: 'TA only', astroOnly: 'Lunar only', combined: 'TA + lunar' };
const date = (value: string) => value.slice(0, 10);
---
<Base title="Zodiacs Desk · Experiment results | Zodiacs" description="Results and limits of a fixed lunar-feature experiment against technical-analysis and simple market baselines." path="/terminal/desk/research/" stableTypography noAssistant privateSurface noindex>
  <article class="lens-report">
    <a href="/terminal/desk/">← Zodiacs Desk</a>
    <header><p class="kicker">A fixed lunar-feature experiment</p><h1>Does the sky layer help?</h1><p class="deck">This experiment found no consistent added predictive benefit from the tested lunar features. Model forecasts remain disabled.</p><p>Retrospective research · generated {date(results.generatedAt)} · Coinbase Exchange daily BTC and ETH</p></header>
    <section aria-labelledby="question"><h2 id="question">What was tested</h2><p>Predict whether the next UTC daily close is higher than the latest finalized close. Compare simple baselines with technical-only, lunar-only, and combined regularized logistic models on identical days.</p><p>Market features use information available at the forecast cutoff. Lunar features are Moon–Sun elongation sine/cosine and fixed proximity flags for new/full phase, calculated with the pinned engine. No journal notes or social posts enter this experiment.</p><p>Training precedes 2021; chronological validation covers 2021–2022; the held-out evaluation covers January 2023 through September 2026. Scaling uses training rows only, label boundaries are purged, and missing daily candles are not filled. Three declared penalties are selected using validation log loss.</p></section>
    {results.assets.map((asset) => <section aria-labelledby={`result-${asset.product}`}>
      <h2 id={`result-${asset.product}`}>{asset.product}</h2>
      <p>{asset.coverage.n.toLocaleString('en')} observed daily bars, {date(asset.coverage.firstBar)}–{date(asset.coverage.lastBar)}; {asset.coverage.missingBars} missing bars within observed coverage. The common holdout contains {asset.scores.combined.n.toLocaleString('en')} days, approximately {asset.approximateLunarCyclesInHoldout.toFixed(1)} lunar cycles.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Held-out forecast scores · lower Brier and log loss are better</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Brier</th><th scope="col">Log loss</th><th scope="col">Direction accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(asset.scores).map(([key, score]) => <tr><th scope="row">{names[key as keyof typeof names]}</th><td>{number(score.brier)}</td><td>{number(score.logLoss)}</td><td>{percent(score.accuracy)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p>The combined model underperformed the persistence baseline. Its primary Brier difference from TA only is {number(asset.comparison.brier.mean)}, with a conservative 97.5% block interval [{asset.comparison.brier.interval975.map(number).join(', ')}].</p>
      <p><strong>Attribution limit:</strong> the two models selected different regularization penalties. The primary comparison therefore cannot isolate lunar information from the effect of regularization.</p>
      <p><strong>Post-hoc diagnostic:</strong> with the same penalty, the combined-minus-TA Brier difference is {number(asset.postHocMatchedPenalty.pairedComparison.brier.mean)}, with a 95% block interval [{asset.postHocMatchedPenalty.pairedComparison.brier.interval95.map(number).join(', ')}]. This interval includes no difference. This check was added after viewing the first holdout and is exploratory.</p>
      <details><summary>Combined-model calibration</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Predicted probability bins and observed positive-close frequency</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Predicted bin</th><th scope="col">Days</th><th scope="col">Mean prediction</th><th scope="col">Observed frequency</th></tr></thead><tbody>{asset.scores.combined.calibration.map((bin) => <tr><th scope="row">{percent(bin.lower)}–{percent(bin.upper)}</th><td>{bin.n}</td><td>{bin.predicted === null ? '—' : percent(bin.predicted)}</td><td>{bin.observed === null ? '—' : percent(bin.observed)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
      <details><summary>Dataset receipt</summary><p class="receipt">SHA-256 {asset.datasetSha256}<br />Retrieved {asset.retrievedFirstAt} through {asset.retrievedLastAt}<br />UTC daily opening timestamps; volume in the base asset.</p></details>
    </section>)}
    <section aria-labelledby="prospective"><h2 id="prospective">The prospective paper protocol</h2><p>A separate 180-day pilot is declared for {date(prospective.start)} through {date(prospective.endExclusive)} (end exclusive). It compares a daily SMA20/SMA50 long-or-cash rule with the same rule restricted to fixed new/full lunar phase windows. Both arms use next-day open-to-close paper trades, with {prospective.feeBpsPerSide} basis points fee and {prospective.slippageBpsPerSide} basis points adverse slippage on each side.</p><p>Decisions must be recorded before execution; missed days cannot be backfilled. Reports include net return, daily-close drawdown, costs and coverage separately for BTC and ETH. Interim output is descriptive. The local runner is prepared; persistent scheduling and independent timestamp witnessing are still unconfigured. No prospective outcome or added predictive benefit is claimed.</p><p class="receipt">Protocol {prospective.experimentId}</p></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="limits"><h2 id="limits">How to read these results</h2><p>Paired block-bootstrap intervals use 30-day blocks and 1,000 deterministic replicates. The 97.5% intervals account conservatively for the two primary asset comparisons. BTC and ETH are correlated, and daily observations are not independent lunar events.</p><ul>{results.limitations.map((limit) => <li>{limit}</li>)}</ul><p>A classification score does not establish trading profitability. This study tests one fixed lunar feature set; it does not establish or refute every astrological method. A protocol change requires a new version and a fresh evaluation plan. Prospective, timestamped paper forecasts and independent review are prerequisites for a public forecasting feature.</p></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="receipt"><h2 id="receipt">Reproducibility</h2><p>Experiment {results.experimentId}. Calculations use {results.engine.engine} {results.engine.version} and {results.engine.ephemeris.name} {results.engine.ephemeris.version}. Raw responses, features, weights, and individual predictions remain outside the public site; display and redistribution rights for the source data still need review before release.</p><p class="receipt">Manifest SHA-256 {results.manifestHash}<br />Model-selection freeze SHA-256 {results.modelSelectionFreezeSha256}</p><p>The repository includes the full report, declared manifest, results, tests, and an offline runner under <code>research/market-lens/</code>. Repeating this holdout checks reproducibility; it does not create a new unseen evaluation.</p><p><a href="/terminal/desk/">Return to Zodiacs Desk →</a></p></section>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
.lens-report { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 64px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; }
a { color: var(--text-2); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
header { margin: 42px 0; } h1 { font: 400 clamp(42px, 6vw, 64px)/1.1 var(--font-serif); letter-spacing: -.03em; margin: 12px 0 20px; }
.deck { font-size: 20px; color: var(--text); } p, li { color: var(--text-2); } section { border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-1); padding: 28px 0 8px; }
h2 { font: 400 32px/1.2 var(--font-serif); margin: 0 0 20px; } strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
.table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; } table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; font: 12px/1.6 var(--font-mono); } caption { text-align: left; font: 13px var(--font-sans); margin-bottom: 15px; color: var(--text-2); }
th, td { white-space: nowrap; padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair-1); } th { font-weight: 500; } td { color: var(--text-2); }
summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 12px 0; color: var(--text-2); } .receipt { overflow-wrap: anywhere; font: 11px/1.9 var(--font-mono); }
li { margin-bottom: 12px; } code { font-size: 12px; }
@media (max-width: 600px) { .lens-report { padding: 24px 16px 48px; } .deck { font-size: 18px; } }
</style>
